584	  /* RollingDigitsText — 2D cash-register digit roll (no blur, no 3D).
585	   *
586	   * ## structure
587	   * Each digit is a WHEEL: a static 0-9 column clipped to one line box and
588	   * positioned by --ds-digit. Around it, every animated unit — wheel or
589	   * grouping separator — is a slot that owns an EXPLICIT width, because that is
590	   * the only thing `width` can animate from and to.
591	   *
592	   * ## why a transition for the roll and an animation for enter/exit
593	   * The roll is a TRANSITION on transform. Re-applying a class that is already
594	   * present does not restart an animation, which is why the original
595	   * keyframe-based roll fired on roughly every other change; a transition on a
596	   * changed value always runs, and an interrupted one retargets from wherever
597	   * the wheel currently sits.
598	   *
599	   * Enter and exit are ANIMATIONS for the mirror-image reason: each runs
600	   * exactly once in an element's life, on mount and on unmount. A mount
601	   * animation needs no JavaScript at all to start — which is what let the
602	   * previous version's double-requestAnimationFrame reveal be deleted outright.
603	   *
604	   * ## why one keyframe pair covers both wheels and separators
