606	   * style, so `from { width: 0 }` resolves its `to` as
607	   * --ui-rolling-digits-digit-width on a wheel and as
608	   * --ui-rolling-digits-separator-width on a separator. Do not add explicit
609	   * `to` widths here; that genericity is the whole trick.
610	   *
611	   * ## the baseline invariant
612	   * The hidden "0" spacer is what makes alignment work without magic numbers:
613	   * it is an ordinary in-flow glyph, so it supplies the wheel's baseline. The
614	   * clip is absolutely positioned against it — exactly 1lh tall — and each of
615	   * the ten column children is also 1lh, so -10% per digit lands precisely. A
616	   * clipped inline-block takes its baseline from its bottom margin edge, which
617	   * is why an `overflow: hidden` wheel could not be aligned at any value of
618	   * 1em. The spacer must stay in flow and stay `visibility: hidden` (never
619	   * `display: none`) for that reason, even though the width is now explicit. */
